Jimmy was behind it all.

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:13.580
Yeah. So they, they changed that.

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:19.360
Uh, and then there was a mode B where, uh, it was basically like a fighting, uh, game,

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:21.760
uh, a la street fighter before street fighter.

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:28.760
Yeah. So they, they kind of fixed one of those things and they added back two players, but the whole,

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:32.040
um, only two enemies on the screen.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:35.660
And even then they were going to be like the same variety of enemies.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:37.540
That's still a thing.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:38.820
And I'm surprised by that.

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:46.760
Yeah. I mean, it seems like there, I mean, I'm sure that there was technical limitations.

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:51.940
Otherwise that wouldn't be a thing, but I, I wouldn't really understand why otherwise.

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:57.700
It's just that we've seen games where like, I mean, I guess maybe now because they've worked

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:02.460
in the two players being able, uh, to be on the same screen that maybe they like, they've

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:03.560
solved that problem.

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:07.060
And they were like, yeah, we don't care about solving the two players, the two enemy thing.

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:09.340
Like that, that's just leave that code as is.

00:07:09.340 --> 00:07:14.660
I also got to imagine just, just guessing this here too, but it's like, this isn't like

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:18.960
a lot of other games that aren't like a beat them up like this, where you're just slashing

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:23.600
at enemies. And there's just like one I've been hit animation and one hit animation.

