00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:35.580
Like there's a lot that like, I feel like the game has to think about for each enemy

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:36.460
as you're doing it.

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:41.340
So like, I wonder if that makes it harder to populate with like a bunch of enemies that

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:43.400
all have to kind of keep track of these animations.

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:52.560
It also could have been like, oh, we can either do two players or we can do multiple, uh, different

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:59.120
varieties. And they didn't want to like change the way it played, uh, if you were in the one or two

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:02.600
player mode, um, or it was just too much work.

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:06.220
Any of these totally random guesses could be true.

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:10.500
Just thinking about how the game works, would you want even more than two enemies?

